{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788191379,"nonce":"UFJfuMwuh/mgXmJcr2qEd01Cw9E=","message":"FIXED on branch `spec/orders-makingfor` (b4d0175, c3fc664, 1c05be1, 1b41ad7).\nRelease build clean, 0 warnings 0 errors. Not yet run in-game — the orchestrator\nowns acceptance; the envelopes are in `accept/32b9e01-orders-makingfor.md`.\n\nVERIFIED AGAINST THE DECOMPILED 1.6 SOURCE, not taken on faith. All four\nconsequences confirmed, by member:\n\n1. `RimWorld/WorkGiver_DoBill.cs` `StartOrResumeBillJob` — confirmed.\n   `ReCheckFailedBillTicksRange` really is `new IntRange(500, 600)` in that\n   file, and the skip clause reads `nextTickToSearchForIngredients` back with\n   no pawn qualifier, so \"whole colony\" is right.\n2. RNG burn — confirmed. `Verse/IntRange.cs` `RandomInRange` is\n   `Rand.RangeInclusive`.\n3. `Verse/DangerUtility.cs` `NormalMaxDanger` — confirmed, `makingFor == p`\n   returns `Danger.Deadly`.\n4. Missing reasons — confirmed, and the \"missing 30 steel\" string is in\n   `RimWorld/WorkGiver_ConstructDeliverResources.cs` `JobOnThing` rather than in\n   `WorkGiver_DoBill`. Without `makingFor` that method also `break`s at the\n   FIRST unavailable resource instead of collecting them all, so the fix widens\n   the reason as well as unlocking it.\n\nWHAT THE ISSUE MISSED — a third surviving side effect, and it is the widest.\n`WorkGiver_DoBill.ShouldSkip` walks every `PotentialBillGiver` on the map asking\nfor `BillStack.AnyShouldDoNow`, which is `Bill_Production.ShouldDoNow` per bill,\nwhich WRITES the scribed `paused` flag on three paths. It short-circuits at the\nfirst doable bill, so the worst case is a colony with nothing doable — where one\n`orders` call touches every bill on the map. `makingFor` does not close it; it\nis click-parity like the other two, so it is disclosed in the header and the\nresult note alongside them. Note the asymmetry it creates with spec 2.4:\n`bills` BANS `ShouldDoNow` outright (WorldSafe Class A) so it can read a stack\nwithout writing it, and `orders` cannot refuse, because the call is inside\nvanilla's `JobOnThing`.\n\nONE CORRECTION. `nextTickToSearchForIngredients` is NOT scribed — `RimWorld/\nBill.cs` `ExposeData` does not touch it. The issue never claimed it was, but the\nneighbouring (correct) claim that `nextJobID` IS scribed makes it easy to read\nthat way. The harm is the colony-wide suppression, not the save.\n\nRESTORE vs NULL. Vanilla nulls unconditionally (`FloatMenuMakerMap.GetOptions`).\nThe fix RESTORES the previous value instead, deliberately: vanilla can null\nbecause it is the only setter and its pass cannot re-enter itself, and we are a\nsecond setter. `prevMakingFor` is null on every real path (verbs drain in\n`GameComponentUpdate`, the float menu builds during OnGUI), so this is identical\nto vanilla's null everywhere except the one case where nulling would clear a\nvalue we did not set.\n\nACCEPTANCE NEEDED A NEW OBSERVABLE. `nextTickToSearchForIngredients` was not\npublished by any verb, so the defect this issue names was not observable from\noutside the game. `bills` now emits `next_ingredient_search_tick` and\n`ingredient_search_cooldown` per bill (plain public-field reads). Consequence\nfor the acceptance: the \"moves by 500-600\" measurement CANNOT be run against\n`main`'s shipped assembly, because the instrument and the fix landed together —\nit needs a one-line repro build, spelled out in the acceptance file. The\nmissing-reason half (bullet 3 of the acceptance) DOES run on the shipped binary\nas a straight `main`-vs-branch pair, and is the cheap check.\n\nDESIGN gains two decisions-log entries and `PawnSafe` gains Class G: the hazard\nis not always a getter. `orders` cited its widget, copied\n`FloatMenuOptionProvider_WorkGivers` clause for clause, called no banned\naccessor, and still mutated — because what it omitted was in the provider's\nCALLER. The rule recorded: reproducing a widget means reading its caller too,\nand grepping every member you invoke for the ambient statics it branches on.","files":null}]}